## Relationship Diagram

```
bin/tally.js
    └── src/index.js          (wires Commander)
            └── commands/index.js   (registers all sub-commands)
                    ├── add.js   ──┐
                    ├── remove.js  ├──▶ lib/storage.js
                    ├── list.js    │         (load / save)
                    └── reset.js ──┘
                                   └──▶ lib/formatter.js
                                              (tables, colors)

tests/
  commands/*.test.js  →  mock storage, test business logic
  lib/*.test.js       →  mock fs/promises, test I/O helpers
```

---

## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| `bin/` is a thin shebang wrapper | Keeps all real logic importable and testable |
| Each command is a factory function | Allows fresh `Command` instances per test run |
| `storage.js` isolated in `lib/` | Commands mock it cleanly without touching the filesystem |
| ESM throughout (`import`/`export`) | Enables `jest.unstable_mockModule` for proper ESM mocking |
| `tests/` mirrors `src/` structure | Easy to locate the test for any source file |

